{"term": "de Wallen", "lang": "nl", "script": "latin", "romanization": null, "category": "sex_work_pornography", "subcategory": "red_light_district", "concept": "red_light_district", "is_novel_concept": false, "register": "slang_neutral", "crude": 5, "technical": 5, "recognition_pct_current": 95, "recognition_pct_peak": 97, "peak_year": null, "regional": "NL", "definition": "Amsterdam's historic red-light district, a network of streets and canal-side alleys in the Oude Centrum where licensed sex workers rent illuminated window booths and operate under municipal gedoogbeleid.", "english_term": "the Wallen (Amsterdam red-light district)", "english_translation_quality": "approximate", "notes": "Proper noun; the most internationally recognizable red-light district in the world; subject to ongoing municipal reduction campaigns since 2008 aimed at shrinking its footprint."}
{"term": "Rosse Buurt", "lang": "nl", "script": "latin", "romanization": null, "category": "sex_work_pornography", "subcategory": "red_light_district", "concept": "red_light_district", "is_novel_concept": false, "register": "slang_neutral", "crude": 8, "technical": 5, "recognition_pct_current": 82, "recognition_pct_peak": 85, "peak_year": null, "regional": null, "definition": "Dutch colloquial term for a red-light district, literally 'rosy/reddish neighbourhood,' used generically for any urban prostitution area in the Netherlands or Belgium.", "english_term": "red-light district", "english_translation_quality": "direct", "notes": "The 'rosse' (ruddy/rosy) alludes to the coloured lighting historically used in sex-work windows; functions as a generic common noun unlike 'de Wallen' which is a specific Amsterdam toponym."}
{"term": "tippelzone", "lang": "nl", "script": "latin", "romanization": null, "category": "sex_work_pornography", "subcategory": "street_prostitution_zone", "concept": "tippelzone", "is_novel_concept": true, "register": "clinical", "crude": 12, "technical": 58, "recognition_pct_current": 62, "recognition_pct_peak": 80, "peak_year": 2000, "regional": "NL", "definition": "A formally designated outdoor area in a Dutch municipality where street prostitution was officially tolerated under gedoogbeleid, typically equipped with on-site sanitation, safe-sex supplies, and social-work access; virtually all Dutch tippelzones were closed between 2003 and 2015.", "english_term": null, "english_translation_quality": "none", "notes": "From 'tippelen' (to walk the streets as a sex worker); Utrecht, Eindhoven, and Amsterdam each operated tippelzones; no direct English equivalent because the Dutch model of geographically bounded, welfare-supported street-prostitution tolerance has no counterpart in English-speaking jurisdictions."}
{"term": "gedoogbeleid", "lang": "nl", "script": "latin", "romanization": null, "category": "sex_work_pornography", "subcategory": "tolerance_policy", "concept": "gedoogbeleid", "is_novel_concept": true, "register": "clinical", "crude": 0, "technical": 78, "recognition_pct_current": 86, "recognition_pct_peak": 91, "peak_year": null, "regional": "NL", "definition": "The Dutch administrative doctrine of formally tolerating but not legalising certain otherwise-illegal activities — principally cannabis retail and prostitution — through deliberate prosecutorial non-enforcement, creating a structured legal grey zone.", "english_term": null, "english_translation_quality": "none", "notes": "From 'gedogen' (to condone/tolerate) + 'beleid' (policy); foundational to the Dutch approach to soft drugs and sex work; frequently glossed in English as 'tolerance policy' but that phrase fails to capture the deliberate maintained legal ambiguity; no structural equivalent exists in anglophone law."}
{"term": "gedoogzone", "lang": "nl", "script": "latin", "romanization": null, "category": "sex_work_pornography", "subcategory": "tolerance_zone", "concept": "gedoogzone", "is_novel_concept": true, "register": "clinical", "crude": 5, "technical": 65, "recognition_pct_current": 63, "recognition_pct_peak": 74, "peak_year": null, "regional": "NL", "definition": "A geographically demarcated area in which Dutch gedoogbeleid is in force, permitting activities — such as prostitution or cannabis sales — that would be prosecuted if they occurred outside the zone's boundaries.", "english_term": null, "english_translation_quality": "none", "notes": "Encompasses both prostitution-specific zones and cannabis retail zones; the concept has no English-language equivalent because anglophone jurisdictions regulate through legalisation or prohibition rather than via spatially bounded non-enforcement."}
{"term": "seksinrichting", "lang": "nl", "script": "latin", "romanization": null, "category": "sex_work_pornography", "subcategory": "brothel", "concept": "brothel", "is_novel_concept": false, "register": "clinical", "crude": 10, "technical": 72, "recognition_pct_current": 44, "recognition_pct_peak": 54, "peak_year": null, "regional": "NL", "definition": "Official Dutch administrative and licensing term for any commercial sex establishment — brothel, sex club, escort agency, or peep show — required to hold a municipal operating permit under the 2000 Wet opheffing bordeelverbod framework.", "english_term": "sex establishment", "english_translation_quality": "approximate", "notes": "Broader than 'brothel': encompasses any licensed sex-commerce venue; emerged as the standard bureaucratic term after the Netherlands lifted its brothel ban in October 2000; used in municipal permit applications and inspection reports."}
