{"term": "seksreclame", "lang": "nl", "script": "latin", "romanization": null, "category": "sex_work_pornography", "subcategory": "sex_work_advertising", "concept": "sex_work", "is_novel_concept": false, "register": "clinical", "crude": 18, "technical": 42, "recognition_pct_current": 54, "recognition_pct_peak": 60, "peak_year": null, "regional": null, "definition": "Advertising for sexual services, including window displays, print listings, and online platforms; a regulated category under Dutch and Belgian law with municipal restrictions on placement, visibility, and content.", "english_term": "sex work advertising", "english_translation_quality": "approximate", "notes": "Used primarily in legislative and policy debate contexts; the regulation of seksreclame has been contentious, particularly regarding window-booth display advertising in de Wallen and the migration of advertising to online platforms."}
{"term": "raamprostitutie", "lang": "nl", "script": "latin", "romanization": null, "category": "sex_work_pornography", "subcategory": "window_prostitution", "concept": "window_prostitution", "is_novel_concept": true, "register": "slang_neutral", "crude": 22, "technical": 48, "recognition_pct_current": 88, "recognition_pct_peak": 92, "peak_year": null, "regional": null, "definition": "Window prostitution: the Benelux practice in which sex workers rent small illuminated street-level booths with glass doors from which they display themselves and negotiate directly with passing clients, particularly associated with Amsterdam's de Wallen but also present in Rotterdam, The Hague, Antwerp, and Brussels.", "english_term": null, "english_translation_quality": "none", "notes": "From 'raam' (window) + 'prostitutie'; the window-booth model is structurally unique to the Netherlands and Belgium and sufficiently distinctive that English-language journalism routinely uses the Dutch term untranslated; Amsterdam has reduced window-booth numbers by roughly 40% since 2008."}
{"term": "prostitutiezone", "lang": "nl", "script": "latin", "romanization": null, "category": "sex_work_pornography", "subcategory": "red_light_district", "concept": "red_light_district", "is_novel_concept": false, "register": "clinical", "crude": 10, "technical": 62, "recognition_pct_current": 60, "recognition_pct_peak": 70, "peak_year": null, "regional": null, "definition": "An officially designated prostitution zone in a Dutch or Belgian municipality; the planning and policy term for the geographic area in which sex-work establishments are legally permitted under local zoning ordinances.", "english_term": "prostitution zone", "english_translation_quality": "approximate", "notes": "More bureaucratic than 'rosse buurt' or 'de Wallen'; appears in municipal zoning plans, environmental-impact assessments, and licensing frameworks rather than in everyday speech."}
