{"term": "seksuele dienstverlening", "lang": "nl", "script": "latin", "romanization": null, "category": "sex_work_pornography", "subcategory": "sex_work", "concept": "sex_work", "is_novel_concept": false, "register": "clinical", "crude": 5, "technical": 78, "recognition_pct_current": 54, "recognition_pct_peak": 60, "peak_year": null, "regional": null, "definition": "The formal Dutch legislative, public-health, and social-work term for the provision of sexual services; the preferred bureaucratic framing of sex work as a professional activity category in official government documents.", "english_term": "sexual services provision", "english_translation_quality": "approximate", "notes": "Highly clinical register; 'dienstverlening' = service provision; used in parliamentary debate, healthcare guidelines, and the Dutch Prostitution Act rather than everyday speech; signals an administrative rather than moral frame for discussing sex work."}
